Dark Phoenix ended in era for the x-men  franchise and unfortunately it didn't  end on a high note from rotten reviews  to disappointing box office receipts  this superhero sequel is far from super  and the writing was on the wall long  before it arrived in theaters here's a  spoiler filled look at why Dark Phoenix  bombed in late January 2019 dark  Phoenix's test screenings bombed  dramatically 20th Century Fox knew they  had to fix it but in spite of extensive  reshoots including major changes to the  climax because of perceived similarities  to the ending of another superhero film  critics still savaged Dark Phoenix which  earned a rotten tomato score so low it's  on par with disasters like 2015's  Fantastic Four 2004's Catwoman and the  Titanic not the movie the actual ship  Brian Talarico at Roger Ebert calms some  things up simply calling the film a  joyless lifeless boring affair that's  not good  even if critical response had been  better Dark Phoenix faced an uphill  battle at the theater thanks to strong  competition from hit films John wick  chapter 3 Disney's live-action remake of  Aladdin and the secret life of pets 2  and with box-office juggernaut Avengers  endgame still in theaters even superhero  fans had other options Dark Phoenix  could have avoided these problems if it  had debuted in February as originally  planned but according to reports Fox  moved it to make room for another bomb  at least domestically Alita battle angel  way to double down guys you could argue  that the fate of Dark Phoenix was sealed  way back in December 2017 when it was  announced that Disney was planning to  acquire 20th Century Fox because that  kind of make Dark Phoenix a lame duck  gross  no not that lame duck  but even Howard benefits from being part  of the Marvel Cinematic Universe these  days superhero fans love shared  universes the idea of bringing the x-men  into the MCU is exciting but it also  made Dark Phoenix seem kind of pointless  as fans really just want to see what the  new Marvel version of the team is going  to look like especially since other than  Logan the quality of the MCU films has  been so much higher than most of Fox's  x-men offerings the x-men series has had  more ups and downs than a rollercoaster  after hitting rock bottom with 2006's  x-men The Last Stand the franchise  rebounded in a big way with the 2011  prequel x-men first class and its  follow-up 2014 ambitious time-travel  epic x-men Days of Future past but  things went sour very fast in 2016 with  x-men apocalypse disappointing fans and  critics alike the film was poorly  received and failed to break even at the  domestic box office earning most of its  money overseas as a result Dark Phoenix  started in a hole to begin with as it  had to convince viewers to return to a  franchise that had already disappointed  them and it clearly failed to do so one  of the most disappointing aspects of  Dark Phoenix is the relative absence of  Quicksilver a fan favorite who stole  scenes in both Days of Future past and  apocalypse Quicksilver is sidelined  early on in Dark Phoenix and gets almost  no screen time  there's not even a resolution to the  long-running subplot that he has  secretly the son of magneto and then  there's the absence of Wolverine on the  one hand Hugh Jackman made it clear that  he's done playing Logan so there's  basically no chance he would have been  in the film eventually you're gonna hang  up the claws and it's gonna make a lot  of people very sad huh on the other hand  well Dark Phoenix really needed him the  only real argument otherwise is the fact  that even Jackman couldn't save things  the last time they made a movie from  this story speaking of that Dark Phoenix  loosely adapts the classic Marvel  storyline the Dark Phoenix saga sound  familiar  it's  Phoenix Phoenix dark Dirk Phoenix well  if it seems familiar it might be because  the same story was also adapted in 2006  as x-men The Last Stand yes despite more  than 55 years worth of stories to choose  from Fox for some reason decided to  adapt the same story twice  even though The Last Stand was widely  disliked by fans and critics alike why  repeat the same mistake it's just weird  with x-men premiering in 2000 and Dark  Phoenix acting as the series finale the  x-men franchise is ending as it's just  about to turn 20 years old it's arguably  ending later than it should have the box  office landscape has changed a lot since  x-men was first released and franchise  fatigue has set in Marvel has the  benefit of multiple franchises you don't  get tired of the Avengers because in  between those films you get the  guardians of the galaxy or a black  panther to mix things up but at Fox it's  all x-men all the time if anything  spin-off hits like Logan and Deadpool  proved just how tired the x-men formula  has become as both of those movies  succeeded by intentionally doing  something different and playing off of  expectations Dark Phoenix on the other  hand is exactly what you thought and  feared it was  it's a sad way for the franchise to end  but it's also a happy occasion for fans  to see the characters move over to the  MCU it's long past due for Marvel's  mutants to come home and realize their  full potential check out one of our  newest videos right here  Plus even more looper videos about your  favorite superheroes are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

